WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.400
Dr. Campbell: Welcome to Module One. I want to start somewhere uncomfortable.

2
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:14.200
I want to start with the assumption that the thing that got you promoted
is not the thing that will keep you effective.

3
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:21.900
In thirty years of working with leaders at Yale, at Norwich, and at the
Air Force Command and Staff College, I have watched a pattern repeat.

4
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:29.500
The technical skill is never the problem. The problem is always character
under pressure, and pressure is the only condition that reveals it.

5
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:36.100
So let me define character in a way you can actually work with,
because the dictionary definition is useless to a practitioner.

6
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:43.800
Character is what you do when the cost of doing the right thing
is real, immediate, and paid by you personally.

7
00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:51.200
Not when it is free. Anyone has character when it is free.
